ed to it's a  little bit ironic that this client came  in pre-covered  and unfortunately this house isn't  finished completely  so they haven't been able to enjoy their  home office  whilst covered was happening but they  will get to enjoy it very very soon  one unique feature they described and  they truly wanted was a kids cooking  bench  this would allow the kids to be able to  help out in the kitchen when the parents  needed some assistance  in addition they wanted to be able to  connect the indoors and the outdoors  seamlessly this meant an entertaining  area from indoor  outdoors from both the backyard and the  front yard  which meant including a winter balcony  into the design of course it is very  standard in australia that everybody  wants at least a two-car garage so this  was also added to the brief so how did i  design  this beautiful home and how did i  address every element of the client's  brief  well let's start by looking at natural  light and letting it be  saturated by light throughout the day as  soon as you walk into the home you're  greeted with a double story  light well for the living and dining  area this means that that space being  north facing  is continuously flooded with light it is  also incorporated with boxed out windows  and louvers which aren't modeled the  clients wanted to be able to entertain  but they had  limited space on the block the block was  only 12 meters by 40 meters long  which meant approximately 480 square  meters  of total land mass by incorporating a  bi-fold door that opened up the entire  living room dining room area  onto the entertaining deck and then  incorporating a wrap around pool around  the side of the premises  it truly gave the indoor outdoor  connection they were looking for  as well as a very unique entertaining  space to be able to tie it back in to  the holiday vibe and the holiday  ambience of this property  tropical trees were planted around the  pool and  the master suite was situated smack bang 